 "label": "Filmed Screen",
 "category": "Stylize",
 "tags": ["look"],
 "version": 1,
 "blurb": "The picture as a camera sees it when pointed at a monitor or a TV: the screen's red, green and blue stripes beat against the camera's own pixels into rainbow moire bands that curve with the lens and the angle of the camera, the blacks glow grey blue, the colour runs cool, one side fades off axis, and a soft band rolls through where the backlight and the shutter fall out of step. Get closer and the moire turns into the visible pixel grid; pull focus off the screen and it melts away.",
